   "text": "## Review Comments\n\n**1. Wrong element selected for provider's facility (correctness) \u2014 Medium**\n`src/Services/FHIR/FhirCareTeamService.php`, in the providers loop:\n```php\n// provider can have more than facility matching... we are only going to grab the first facility for now\n$dataRecordProvider = end($dataRecordProviderList);\n```\nThe comment says \"grab the first facility\" but `end()` returns the **last** element of the array. This will silently pick the wrong provider/facility pairing whenever a provider has more than one match. Should be `reset($dataRecordProviderList)` or `$dataRecordProviderList[0]`.\n\n**2. Fragile code-system detection for facility taxonomy \u2014 Low/Medium**\n```php\nif ($codeParts[0] === \"SNOMED-CT\") {\n    $roleCoding->setSystem(FhirCodeSystemUris::SNOMED_CT);\n} else {\n    $roleCoding->setSystem(FhirCodeSystemUris::NUCC_PROVIDER);\n}\n```\nThis defaults silently to NUCC for anything that isn't exactly `\"SNOMED-CT\"` (case-sensitive match on a free-text/legacy column, flagged by the author's own TODO about column size). Any other prefix, casing variant, or malformed value will be mis-tagged as NUCC rather than surfaced as an error or \"unknown\" \u2014 producing incorrect FHIR output without warning.\n\n**3. Inconsistent fallback when code description lookup fails \u2014 Low**\nFor providers, when `lookup_code_descriptions()` returns empty, the code falls back to `xlt($dataRecordProvider['role_title'])`. For facilities, the equivalent branch just sets `$description = null`, which means `roleCoding->setDisplay(null)` with no fallback title. This inconsistency looks unintentional and will produce Codings with no `display` for facilities where provider participants would still have one.\n\n**4. Unchecked array index on `$dataRecord['status']` \u2014 Low**\n```php\nif (array_search($dataRecord['status'], self::CARE_TEAM_STATII) !== false) {\n```\nIf `status` is not set on the data record (e.g. older records, partial joins), this throws a PHP notice/warning. An `isset()`/`??` guard would be safer, consistent with falling back to `active` by default.\n\n**5. Behavior change in `searchForOpenEMRRecords` not explained \u2014 Medium**\n```php\n-        return $this->careTeamService->getAll($openEMRSearchParameters, false, $puuidBind);\n+        return $this->careTeamService->getAll($openEMRSearchParameters, true, $puuidBind);\n```\nThe second argument (presumably an AND/OR toggle for combining search criteria) was flipped with no comment or test demonstrating the new multi-parameter search (e.g. `patient` + `status`) behaves correctly. Worth double-checking test coverage for combined search parameters introduced in this same PR (`patient`, `status`, `_id`).\n\n**6. Naming inconsistency: `USCGI_PROFILE_URI` vs `IResourceUSCIGProfileService` \u2014 Low (cosmetic)**\nThe class implements `IResourceUSCIGProfileService` but defines `const USCGI_PROFILE_URI`. The letters are transposed (USCGI vs USCIG). This is likely a typo and could cause confusion/maintenance errors if other services follow a different (correct) naming convention for this constant.\n\n**7. Minor duplication/maintainability**\nThe `FHIRCodeableConcept`/`FHIRCoding` construction logic for \"known role\" vs \"data-absent reason\" is duplicated almost identically in both the provider and facility loops. Extracting a small helper (e.g. `buildRoleCodeableConcept($code, $title, $system)`) would reduce duplication and the risk of the two branches drifting out of sync.\n\n**8. Stylistic nits**\n- `CARE_TEAM_STATII` is an odd pluralization (status \u2192 statuses); minor readability issue.\n- Several added blank double-lines (e.g. around the new `const` and after the facilities loop) are unnecessary noise.\n\nNo security issues were found (no raw SQL/user input concatenation visible here), and the removal of the redundant `getOne()` override in favor of the base class implementation looks reasonable given the newly added `_id` search parameter \u2014 just worth confirming via tests that `CareTeamService::getAll` correctly filters by `uuid` through the new `ServiceField`."
